{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YEoPERYX69EsJvk6sqbM8Q","type":"tool_result","content":"218\t\n219\t## GM answer conventions learned\n220\t- Submit the slug ONLY, exactly as decoded (lowercase, hyphens, 2-digit number). Not the whole sentence and not \"Game Master: ...\". `trim` normalization only.\n221\t- No correctly decoded warmups answer has been rejected (days 1-28; day 8's 40 and day 9's 45 slugs all accepted as decoded). The only `incorrect` (day 7 mastery set1) was a wrong value from decoding the whole bundle. The value is self-describing, so verify it against `answer_format.syntax` and submit.\n222\t- Mastery ids are per set (`setN.message` style). Each question names `blob-0N.txt`, but the bytes may arrive as a zip member, as same-named `blob.txt` downloads, or de-duplicated (`blob_2.txt`). Map set -> file by sha256 from `contract[\"artifacts\"]` when present. When it is absent (day 7), open the zip and read member `blob-0N.txt`.\n223\t- No GM-side label grammar in this lane: the answer is a derived VALUE, never a synthetic label.\n224\t\n225\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n226\t- DELIVERY: Mastery = ONE zip saved as `blob-01.txt` (check magic, not extension); read member `blob-0N.txt`, never the\n227\t  bundle (D7: a slug that is a word suffix `py-...` is the tell). Missing set bytes = a downloader problem (D1, ~12 fails),\n228\t  not a solver one. Dry runs on renamed per-set copies do NOT reproduce the real layout: test on the raw delivery.\n229\t- NEVER REPLACE THE LANE SOLVER (D21): copy the previous day's warmups `solve.py` and add the new codec as ONE branch\n230\t  (whole-blob step + `register_free(name, day, fn)`). A fresh generic brute-force solver passes single/TT (one short\n231\t  blob) and then dies at 60 s on Mastery (103 sets x 21 lines). A prebuilt lib codec is equally useless if the carried\n232\t  solver never routes to it (D18 `rail_solve`). First move on a new day: lib's whole-blob candidates (`decode_chunk` +\n233\t  `warmups_codecs.CANDIDATES`/`*_solve`).\n234\t- CHEAP PATH FIRST, RETURN EARLY (D17): return the first candidate that yields a full slug; call the joint ranker only on\n235\t  a miss (83 x 17 passed 60 s when every set paid the joint search; a per-set `peel` BFS blew a 30 s window on D12). Time\n236\t  the real Mastery case (`hctf solver-test`) after every new codec; profile `answer()` per set when solve passes ~5 s.\n237\t- PRE-DECODING / MIS-REGISTERED MASTERY LINES (D23 113/113, D25 123/123 sets wrong once; D26 60 s kill; D27 34.9 s):\n238\t  never rewrite a numbered line to plaintext before `decode_chunked`/`_joint_free` (no \"identity\" choice: ROT5 turned\n239\t  `el-46` into `el-91`); register today's codec on the RAW line even if the whole-blob path decodes it; a DAYS encoder\n240\t  that doesn't reproduce the GM bytes is worse than none (see Variant axes: line wrapper). All sets wrong in the same\n241\t  field = one line's routing. D28: no day-28 codec, saved only by being the LAST line -> register `(28, \"revhex\",\n242\t  lambda s: s.encode().hex()[::-1], lambda t: bytes.fromhex(t[::-1]).decode(), False)` before line 28 is a middle line.\n243\t- ENGLISH SCORING: don't count single letters/hex reads as English (D3 timeout); a rot-N must beat the unshifted text by a\n244\t  margin (D4). Rot-N is `decode_chunk`'s catch-all, so ANY unknown plain transform comes back as plausible rot garbage\n245\t  (D12 reversal `69-fove-n`, D13's rejected `ovisx-tviskr-fbvecw-31` = rot-N of Atbash): gibberish slug words = an unknown\n246\t  transform, not a GM quirk. Several free transforms in one blob (rot13/rev/Atbash/Caesar/ROT47) -> decide JOINTLY, each\n247\t  once (`_joint_free`), rank full 3-word slugs first (D14 set22); prune by alphabet before the joint search (D15)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93819e34-795d-46dc-ac6a-56c07da4c6a6","uuid":"4314e762-93c4-44ba-ae96-0a32b654312c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:42:34.723Z","tool_use_res