friend\" verbatim; D29-D30 stayed\n33\t  REMIXES (rot13 over base64; url over url): three 2-layer stacks of D1-D12 codecs in a row, each cued by a riddle\n34\t  naming an old codec (a number, \"address bar\") + a combining word (\"invited ... over\", \"twice\"). On an unknown\n35\t  shape read the blob's STRUCTURE (repeating unit, token shape, a tiny alphabet of operators/words) and name the spec\n36\t  from it + the pun; a prompt that QUOTES an old day's riddle = that day's codec is one of the layers.\n37\t- Mastery is cumulative: day N = 5N-2 sets x N numbered lines `NN<TAB>fragment`, line k = day k's encoding (D26 line =\n38\t  a 166-217 B BF program printing a 5-char tail; D27 line = 1672-2172 B of Ook printing a 4-5 char tail; D28 line = 8\n39\t  (136/138) or 10 reversed-hex chars = a 4-5 char tail; D29 line = 8-char rot13'd padded base64 `nJkfoj==`; D30 line =\n40\t  36 chars of doubled percent `%25%37%37%25%32%64...` = a 4-char tail; 148 x 30).\n41\t  Last line has no trailing newline; fragments split mid-word and join verbatim.\n42\t- Clocks: D1-D15 TT ~5-8 s / Mastery ~5-9 s windows; since D16 mostly `deadline: null`. The HARNESS kills solve.py at\n43\t  60 s regardless (D17, D21, D26 128 x 26: 0 answers, a live worker hand-decoded). D23/D25 Mastery first submit all-NN\n44\t  wrong (pre-decoded line), fixed on the same attempt. D27 Mastery 133 x 27 solve 34.9 s (bad DAYS encoder). D28 TT 5.1 s\n45\t  (solve 1.05 s), Mastery 138 x 28 9.3 s (solve 6.2 s), both first try. D29 TT 2.4 s, Mastery 143 x 29 4.9 s, first\n46\t  try. D30 TT 3.0 s; Mastery 148 x 30 solve 65.9 s -> KILLED (line 30 pre-peeled, no DAYS[29]/[30]); a live worker's\n47\t  plain positional table (line k -> day k's decoder, 30 entries) got 148/148 on its first submit.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93819e34-795d-46dc-ac6a-56c07da4c6a6","uuid":"3667b4b7-6da8-4013-a5aa-5dec1331bcf0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:42:53.628Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/h